// Events found by exploring (the Explore button in a zone). `repeat` says when
// an event can come back: once, until resolved ("~ resolve"), or always.

// A one-off find that moves the quest along (characters/wren.fsc).
== event glint_in_the_moss
name: Something glinting
found by: exploring in forest
repeat: until resolved
// Only while Wren is looking for her knife.
requires: quest lost_knife is asked
play:
    Something glints in the moss beside the path.
    * Pick it up
        It is a small carving knife, its handle worn smooth. This must be Wren's.
        ~ give carving_knife
        ~ resolve
    * Leave it
        You leave it where it lies. Someone might be missing it, though.

// Picking a random creature: the scene names one that lives here, without a fight.
== event rustling_bushes
name: Rustling bushes
found by: exploring in forest, riverbank
repeat: always
play:
    ~ pick random creature tagged woodland nearby
    if a creature is picked:
        The bushes rustle and part. [A picked creature] peers out at you, then thinks better of it and vanishes.
    else:
        The bushes rustle, but nothing comes out.

// A fight with a branch for each outcome; `outcomes` names the results an event
// can record ("~ outcome made_friends"), which other content can test
// ("river_crossing outcome is made_friends").
== event river_crossing
name: The stepping stones
found by: exploring in riverbank
repeat: until resolved
outcomes: made_friends, chased_off
play:
    A line of stepping stones crosses the river. An otter sits on the middle one, guarding it.
    * Shoo it away
        fight river_otter:
            won:
                The otter gives up the stone with a sulky chirp. You cross without getting your feet wet.
                ~ outcome chased_off
                ~ resolve
            lost:
                You slip off a stone and land in the shallows with a splash.
                ~ hurt 2
            fled:
                You back off the stones. The otter looks smug.
    * Offer it a berry [if player has wild_berries]
        ~ take wild_berries
        The otter takes the berry with both paws, considers you, and moves aside.
        ~ outcome made_friends
        ~ give lucky_acorn
        ~ resolve
    * Leave
        You leave the otter to its stone.

// An event that starts a captivity (events/brambles.fsc defines it).
== event bramble_patch
name: A bramble patch
found by: exploring in riverbank
repeat: always
play:
    You push through a thicket by the water, and the brambles close around your legs.
    play bramble_snare
    You pick the last thorns out of your trousers.

// Found by scavenging (rules/scavenging.fsc), not by exploring.
== event forgotten_basket
name: A forgotten basket
found by: scavenging in forest
repeat: once
play:
    Half-hidden under a fern is an old wicker basket. Inside: a clean bandage and a slingshot.
    ~ give bandage
    ~ give slingshot
